Hi, Vicki -

You may find the kpath.census function in sna to be helpful here; see, 
in particular, the path.comembership and/or dyadic.tabulation options.  
This will allow you to (among other things) identify pairs of nodes 
joined by paths of particular lengths.  (See also kcycle.census and 
geodist.)

Hope that helps,

-Carter

