> > is a binary attribute indicating if they share any club membership or
> not).
>
> i would think you might be more interested in a quantitative measure of
> how many club memberships they have in common.
>
> > Is there a way to introduce such a term into an ERGM model (and
> represent it as a node attribute of type
> > list) or that I have to add a separate nodal attribute for each club and
> introduce a nodematch("<club>")
> > term for each club?
>
> you can create a dyad covariate that takes the value 1 if they share any
> club memberships, but you'll need to do this outside of the ergm call.
> it's a data processing step that will use the utilities in R and the
> network package.
>
> > An alternative way to think about it whether it is possible to have a
> term representing *another
> > network* N2, hypothesizing that a (weighted?) tie in N2 increases the
> likelihood of observing a tie in
> > the network in question.
> >
> > Thanks again!
