Message-ID: <DD8B773F302EA644B1169B18D744F40D85D242E9@xmail32.ad.ua.ac.be>

Dear all,

I am trying to calculate a matrix of probabilities (C = Cij) estimated from the logistic regression in the adjacency matrix Rij. The pstar function in SNA gives you a GLM object with estimated probabilities after estimation. For example:

model1=pstar(dat = network_economy2005, effects=c("choice", "mutuality"), diag = TRUE)
prob_basis=matrix(model1$fitted.values, nrow = 212, ncol=212)

Now, I'd like to do the same with the function ERGM. This doesn't seem to be straightforward, however. ERGM is a logistic regression model, with p = exp(XB)/(1+exp(XB)), so in theory it should be possible to estimate predicted probabilities. In practice, however, I can't find how to do this.

Could anyone give me some advice on this?

Many thanks,

Best, Mathias
PhD Candidate, University of Antwerp (Belgium)
